<p>Cuba began restoring electricity on Sunday after another nationwide grid collapse left millions without power, with service returning first in parts of Havana and some outlying provinces. State utility updates said the shutdown of a major power plant in Nuevitas, Camaguey province, on Saturday evening triggered a cascade failure across the island&#x27;s grid. The blackout was the second full grid failure in a week and, by some accounts, the third nationwide collapse this month, underscoring the strain on Cuba&#x27;s aging energy system and deep fuel shortages. Several outlets said Cuban officials blamed the broader energy crisis on a U.S. oil blockade that has eroded fuel supplies and generation capacity, while crews worked to bring key plants back online and reconnect hospitals, homes and businesses.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/2PtwlsM0V9BdemXrTzRUBlGW9ByfaOc4IHdeICZh2oBdVycveXBnAgnzDyD2FSxGvYpbIqonsMTJplKoDHsOJOqwrp-Wl9Hn0FRK65lGA1cKBz3ciH3hx77uttI8AY4CrsN0JBrsGPPfhz9c4uv3YNrupZk888EY-HoPNSr0mmEISYQnKiVW434lo9VT_nySqgeUDLi6OgBQQ-UpHCo9ZVkGUI-f-HZ56j3RfobA_Tb4Ot42grQCVzhwSJSRduMtt3F0LpsHPIp2QQd8bRzgFfeLuL-1l0vb2QO6GSE9y0Wsj_qPgRm7zlFMJP5DiGgwipWIBqpk6-KWqAFxY374cLL52EOoERSdpiV1kccp0845525imfpBbkfSq1f6sjnmvjW6ig9xbDsfi8B62NzOZGxk0YF9gZkEZittxQjJ65yLC6PsAljD7LDvEsTw9ALAn2Vmomg57smiNhlBENJKhF7z-DPaOxoKHAS5w41k3ME' alt='Scene from Cuba&#x27;s power restoration effort after the nationwide blackout.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Havana recovery: By Sunday afternoon, nearly 500,000 homes and businesses in Havana — about 55% of the capital&#x27;s total — had power again, and 43 hospitals were back online, according to the Electric Union.</li><li>Early reconnections: Earlier in the day, officials said electricity had already returned to about 72,000 customers in Havana, including five hospitals, as restoration efforts picked up pace.</li><li>Fuel constraint: Officials said a severe diesel shortage meant only part of the grid&#x27;s generation capacity was available, so many areas could still face lengthy blackouts even after the network restarts.</li><li>Daily disruption: Residents in Havana told reporters that recurring outages have become so routine that some households cook with firewood several times a week when the power goes out.</li></ul><blockquote>We’re stuck ​in the same rut. It’s absolute madness. There’s no other way around it. - Leoni Alberto</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cuban Electric Union: The state grid operator said it was preparing to restart the country&#x27;s largest oil-fired power plant and expected that move to sharply raise generation by the end of Sunday. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/cuba-restores-power-to-havana-after-grid-collapse/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li><li>Cuban government and state media: Officials described the blackout as another consequence of fuel shortages tied to the U.S. oil blockade, saying external pressure has further weakened an already fragile energy system. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0l44yxrvo'>BBC News</a>)</li><li>Havana residents: Some residents said repeated outages have become part of daily life in the capital, forcing households to improvise basic tasks such as cooking during long interruptions. (<a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/cuba-restores-power-to-havana-after-grid-collapse/'>Michael West Media</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/cuba-nationwide-power-grid-collapse-restoration/'>Cuba begins to restore electricity after nationwide power grid collapse</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://michaelwest.com.au/cuba-restores-power-to-havana-after-grid-collapse/'>Cuba restores power to Havana after grid collapse</a> - michaelwest.com.au</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg0l44yxrvo'>National blackout hits Cuba for second time in a week</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-cuba-works-to-restore-power-after-second-grid-collapse-in-a-week/'>Cuba works to restore power after second grid collapse in a week</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/cuba-begins-restore-power-after-nationwide-grid-collapse-131304306'>Cuba begins to restore power after nationwide grid collapse</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/cuba-begins-to-restore-power-after-third-nationwide-collapse-in-month/article70774192.ece'>Cuba begins to restore power after third nationwide collapse in month</a> - thehindu.com</li></ul>